@flexiarg features/emit-per-tick-mismatch
@title Emit the Per-Tick Mismatch, and Replay Without It
@style implementation-pattern
@why war-room/wr-27-a-loop-is-born-instrumented-for-its-gain
@holds-at R8
@builds-from problems/per-tick-mismatch-instruments-outer-loop-gain
@audience whoever picks up C-R8
@tone plain-operational
@references [problems/per-tick-mismatch-instruments-outer-loop-gain aif/present-fit-mismatch]
@status [status[specified] blocked-by[none]]

! conclusion:
  Write the per-tick mismatch into the attempt record as a checkpoint field,
  route it into the outer-loop update, and prove it is READ by replaying the
  same ticks with the value frozen.

  + context: The mission-conditional-reward outer loop is supposed to consume
    returned reward. Nothing records the quantity it would consume. This is the
    build behind C-R8; the problem statement is
    problems/per-tick-mismatch-instruments-outer-loop-gain and the promotion
    test is p4ng/empirics-futon/promotion-tests.edn.

  + IF:
    A loop returns reward and an update consumes it.

  + HOWEVER:
    The mismatch is not in the record. 62 archived attempts across
    wm-outer-loop-40-v1 through -46-v1 carry seven checkpoints each --
    time-step, selection, construction, dispatch, build, adjudication, closed --
    and no gain reading in any of them. The only gain-shaped token in the whole
    archive is `:tau-mode :selection-gain-only`, which is a configuration flag
    and not a value. So the loop cannot be shown to read a quantity that was
    never written, and the ring restates itself: the defect is visible only to
    whoever reads the per-tick mismatch.

  + THEN:
    Emit the mismatch as a field on the attempt's own checkpoints, carrying its
    provenance the way `:selection-source` already distinguishes an operator
    pick from the selector's (full_loop_runner.clj). Route it into the
    outer-loop update. Then run the same tick sequence twice, once live and
    once with the mismatch held at a constant, and record both action
    sequences.

  + BECAUSE:
    WR-27 asks that a loop be born instrumented for its gain, and a value that
    is recorded but not read is the current state wearing an instrument. The
    replay is what separates those two, and it is the only part of this that
    cannot be satisfied by writing more fields.

  + FAILURE-MODES:
    - Instrument theatre: the mismatch is emitted, nothing consumes it, and the
      board reports the ring closed because a field appeared.
    - Replay without a control: one run is recorded and the difference is
      argued from the mechanism. The frozen-value run is the whole test.
    - Cohort contamination: wm-outer-loop-40-v1's next eligible opportunity is
      `attempt-002`, held open for a defect repair that is independently
      reviewed, canaried and marked with a new semantic epoch
      (archives/stop-line-2026-07-15/README.md). A hand-driven run under that
      id consumes a pre-registered slot without meeting its conditions. Use a
      new cohort id.
    - Ghost arming: `GET /api/alpha/war-machine` starts the in-process
      scheduler as a side effect of being read, at a 300s period, so ticks can
      arrive that nobody asked for. A measurement run must know which ticks are
      its own.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Name the field and where it is written -- one checkpoint, not five.]
    next[State the constant the null control freezes the mismatch AT, and why
         that value rather than another; a frozen value is a choice and an
         unexamined one can make the control pass.]
    next[Pick the tick run to replay and record its cohort id before running.]
